Update function:

```
function update(dt) {
  time += dt;
  if (state !== 'playing') { updateAmbient(dt); return; }
  if (crashTimer > 0) { updateCrash(dt); updateParticles; return; }
  updateBike(dt);
  updateParticles(dt);
  updateCamera(dt);
  updateScore(dt);
  audio.engine(...)
}
```

updateBike:

```
const gas = input.gas, brake = input.brake;
const speed = Math.abs(bike.vx);
if (bike.onGround) {
  const slope = terrain.slopeAt(bike.x);
  let accel = 0;
  if (gas) accel += 780;
  if (brake) accel -= 1500;
  bike.vx += accel * dt;
  bike.vx += 1000 * Math.sin(slope) * dt; // gravity along slope
  bike.vx *= Math.exp(-0.9*dt); // drag
  bike.vx = clamp(bike.vx, -220, MAX_SPEED);
  // move
  const prevAngle = bike.angle;
  bike.x += bike.vx*dt;
  // slope now
  const xr = bike.x - Math.cos(bike.angle)*WHEELBASE/2;
  const xf = bike.x + Math.cos(bike.angle)*WHEELBASE/2;
  const gy = (terrain.yAt(xr)+terrain.yAt(xf))/2;
  const slopeNow = Math.atan2(terrain.yAt(xf)-terrain.yAt(xr), Math.max(1, xf-xr));
  const restY = gy - WHEEL_R;
  // launch check: if terrain fell away faster than we can follow
  if (restY > bike.y + 6 && Math.abs(bike.vx) > 60) {
     bike.onGround = false;
     bike.vy = bike.vx * Math.tan(prevAngle); // carry momentum
     bike.angVel = 0;
     bike.airRot = 0;
     bike.airTime = 0;
     audio.jump();
     spawnDust(...);
  } else {
     bike.y = restY;
     bike.vy = 0;
     bike.angle = approachAngle(bike.angle, slopeNow, 1-Math.exp(-16*dt));
     bike.wheelSpin += bike.vx*dt/WHEEL_R;
     bike.susp = Math.max(0, bike.susp - dt*6); // ?
     // dust
  }
} else {
  // air
  bike.airTime += dt;
  bike.vy += GRAVITY*dt;
  bike.x += bike.vx*dt;
  bike.y += bike.vy*dt;
  // torque
  let torque = 0;
  if (gas) torque -= 5.0;
  if (brake) torque += 5.0;
  bike.angVel += torque*dt;
  bike.angVel *= Math.exp(-0.35*dt);
  bike.angle += bike.angVel*dt;
  bike.airRot += bike.angVel*dt;
  bike.wheelSpin += bike.vx*dt/WHEEL_R*0.5;
  // land
  const gy = groundAt(bike.x, bike.angle);
  if (bike.y + WHEEL_R >= gy) {
     const slope = slopeAt...
     const diff = angleDiff(bike.angle, slope);
     if (Math.abs(diff) > 1.05) crash();
     else land(gy, slope, diff);
  }
}
```

Careful launch check condition: restY > bike.y + 6 means ground is lower (larger y) than current rest position → drop. At crest, after moving forward, ground drops, restY increases. Bike.y currently old ground - R. So yes. But on downhill, restY might be slightly larger each frame, triggering launch constantly even at moderate slopes. Threshold 6px per frame at 60fps = 360px/s drop; at speed 400 and slope 0.9, drop ~? tan(0.9)=1.26 → 500px/s = 8px/frame. So steep downhill launches—fine. But threshold should scale with dt: `restY - bike.y > Math.max(4, 250*dt)`. At 60fps 4px. Hmm downhill slope 0.2 at 400px/s = 80px/s = 1.3px/frame → no launch. Good.

Also when launching, bike.vy = vx * tan(prevAngle). If angle negative (uphill), vy negative → up. Good. But if bike.y snaps to restY and restY > old y, the launch occurs at old y, which is above ground → looks like flying off crest. Good.

Landing: need to set bike.y = gy - WHEEL_R and angle to slope, onGround true; vy=0; vx *= 0.94. Compute flips from airRot. Crash if bad angle. Also detect if bike hits ground while upside down.

Landing threshold 1.0 rad ~57° relative. Good.

Also if bike.y + R >= gy but bike is below terrain (tunnel) — same.

