Patch resize to build backdrop and groundGrad, and fixed timestep loop. Also update ground gradient creation in resize (needs ctx). Add after BIKE_SCALE.

```
paintBackdrop();
groundGrad = ctx.createLinearGradient(...); stops...
```
But groundGrad uses main ctx and fixed y; fine.

Fixed timestep: modify frame.

```
const FIXED_DT = 1/60;
let acc = 0;
function frame(now){
  let delta=(now-last)/1000;
  last=now;
  if (!isFinite(delta)||delta<0) delta=0;
  delta=Math.min(delta,0.2);
  acc+=delta;
  let steps=0;
  while(acc>=FIXED_DT && steps<12){ update(FIXED_DT); acc-=FIXED_DT; steps++; }
  if(steps===12) acc=0;
  render();
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
}
```
Potential issue: on 5fps, each frame 12 steps * 1/60 = 0.2s; update's audioTick etc fine. DOM updateHud 12 times but cached.

Menu time updates 12 steps per frame → cloud animation smooth.

Also after startGame `last = performance.now()`; acc may hold leftover from menu; reset acc=0 in start/pause/resume. Declare `let acc=0;`. Since startGame defined before acc declaration? Function hoisted, variable `let acc` declared later in file but used at call time after initialization—fine as long as declaration executes before startGame called (it will, at boot end). But `startGame` is called only via user after boot. Add acc=0 there.

Let me patch.

