content.text:
0.38ms per frame synchronously!? That means the render itself is fast (canvas commands are async/queued; SwiftShader rasterizes later). The bottleneck is likely compositing/rasterization, not JS commands. 0.38ms JS means rendering is cheap; GPU (software) raster is slow at 1280x800 with gradients and paths.

Given raster-bound, reducing resolution is the only lever. But 9fps in headless software is expected; real hardware will be 60. The game is playable on real devices.

However, we should still make the menu not 3fps: remove backdrop-filter (blur is costly in software). Replace with slightly darker background. Do that.

